node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
.orchestra/

# agent worktrees (ephemeral, created by the Agent tool isolation)
.claude/worktrees/

# `.atlas` CAS/projection are local rebuildable state. Never commit model-derived store bytes.
# Deny every child by default; only reviewed configuration and append-only shared logs travel.
# `.atlas/` itself stays visible so later explicit exceptions remain possible.
.atlas/*
# `memory.jsonl` — the per-seat Memory log. MEM-10a REQUIRES it to travel at every commit / PR / branch /
# fork, so it is admitted like the projection is. It is safe to admit for a reason the projection cannot
# claim: the file is append-only and content-keyed one record per line (KERNEL-12b/12c), so a plain git text
# merge can only union or duplicate whole lines — never splice two records — and a duplicate is deduped by
# content id on the fold. There are no numbered generations to drag in, because nothing is ever replaced.
!.atlas/memory.jsonl
# `orientation.jsonl` — the derived-channel event log the Orientation slab folds. Admitted for a REQUIREMENT,
# not a convenience: MEM-6 says the slab is byte-identical across all members, members work in different
# clones, so a log that stayed local would fold to a different Orientation per machine and the invariant
# would be false by construction. Same append-only content-keyed form, same safe line merge.
!.atlas/orientation.jsonl
# `review.jsonl` — the shared review log (holds, ratification proposals and decisions, interview answers, memory
# proposals; specs/atlas-ui/build/DECISIONS.md D14). Same append-only, content-keyed one-record-per-line form as the
# two logs above, so a union merge can only add whole lines; a hold or a decision must survive a merge.
!.atlas/review.jsonl
# The tree that replaces the three single files above (`packages/adapter-io/src/layout.ts`): shared logs under
# `project/`, each seat's memory and knowledge logs under `members/<seat>/`. Same append-only content-keyed form.
# The legacy single files stay admitted until `atlas migrate-layout` has moved their lines.
!.atlas/project/
!.atlas/members/
# The CAS bytes each knowledge row names (`.atlas/blobs/<h[0:2]>/<h>`), so a fresh clone can replay the rows. They
# are copies of door outputs, never a store: `cas/` and the projection stay local, and replay re-checks every hash.
!.atlas/blobs/
# …and the admin-owned policy, as before: the ratified config the doors READ, reviewable in the same place
# as the code.
!.atlas/policy.json

# staging must never travel at ANY depth. The root-anchored `.atlas/*` above only matches the repo-root
# store; test runs create scratch `.atlas/` dirs under packages/*/ (e.g. packages/grounding/.atlas/) whose
# staging*.json slips that anchor. This unanchored rule denies staging everywhere — same intent as above,
# closing the nested-dir gap so `git add -A` after a test run cannot drag candidate material into history.
**/.atlas/staging*.json

# runtime telemetry from the orchestrator harness — not product source
.maestro/
